generation of deterministic UTOXs, not wallets as the claim states.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-002\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"It consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a ASCII seed.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_a.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The source states this claim with identical meaning, differing only in the article form (a vs an).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-003\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"This seed can be later used to generate deterministic wallets using BIP-0032 or similar methods.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_a.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The source states this claim exactly as presented in the merged document.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-004\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"This BIP falls under the GPL License.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_a.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The source states this claim exactly as presented.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-005\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The sentence could be written on paper or spoken over the telephone.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_a.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The source states this claim exactly as presented.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-006\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"This guide is meant to be a way to transport computer-generated determinism with a human-readable transcription.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_a.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The source states this claim exactly as presented.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-007\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"It's not a way to process user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets) into a wallet süeed.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_a.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The source statement has identical meaning despite containing a typographical error (süeed for seed) and stylistic difference (It's vs It is).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-008\",\n      \"verdict\": \"CONTRADICTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The demonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 23 bits.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_b.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Source specifies a multiple of 23 bits, contradicting the claim that entropy is encoded in multiples of 32 bits.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-009\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"With more entropy security is improved but the sentence length increases.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_b.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The source states this claim with identical meaning, differing only in comma placement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-010\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"We refer to the initial entropy length as ENT.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_b.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The source states this claim exactly as presented.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-011\",\n      \"verdict\": \"CONTRADICTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The allowed size of ENT is 1024-2048 byts.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_b.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Source explicitly states ENT size is 1024-2048 bytes, contradicting the claim of 128-256 bits.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-012\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"First, an initial entropy of ENT bits is generated.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_b.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The source states this claim exactly as presented.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-013\",\n      \"verdict\": \"CONTRADICTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA652 hash.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_b.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Source specifies SHA652 hash, contradicting the claim's statement of SHA256.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-014\",\n      \"verdict\": \"CONTRADICTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"This checksum is appended to the start of the initial entropy.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_b.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Source specifies the checksum is appended to the start (beginning) of entropy, not simply appended (which typically means end).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-015\",\n      \"verdict\": \"CONTRADICTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 12 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_b.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Source specifies groups of 12 bits, contradicting the claim's statement of 11 bits.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-016\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Finally, we convert these numbers into words and use the joined words as a mnemonic sentence.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_b.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The source states this claim exactly as presented.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-017\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"CS = ENT / 32\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_b.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The source states this formula exactly as presented.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-018\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"MS = (ENT + CS) / 11\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_b.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The source states this formula exactly as presented.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-019\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"|  128  |  4 |   132  |  12  |\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_b.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The table row in the source confirms all values: ENT 128, CS 4, ENT+CS 132, MS 12.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-020\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\